      "changesetId": 146375270,
      "finding": "The survey-and-imagery-tagged mapper deliberately normalizes this residential way to Touil Ouled Zayed while preserving the same Arabic place name, creates the same-named place=hamlet node, and assigns the name to a separately typed natural=peak. The three exact per-object edits are present in the actual OSC.",
      "interpretation": "The residential area was already explicitly named as an inhabited land-use area by the earlier mapper. The later mapper reaffirms that same named residential identity and adds its same-named hamlet representation, while using natural=peak for the separate landform. This supports a common settlement identity for the two inhabited-place representations; it is more specific than timestamps or proximity alone.",
      "limit": "The source declaration is changeset-wide and mapper-provided. It does not independently prove which specific facts were observed on the ground, and contains no textual assertion or relation enumerating the hamlet footprint."
    },
